# The matrix cases that disagree with the pinned SQLite 3.53.4 because of a
# defect that is not fixed yet.
#
# One per line: the case id, a tab, the bug's number in the description of
# task-2136 ("Inillucent Test Suite Bugs Found"), a tab, and one sentence.
#
# A listed case that still disagrees passes. A listed case that now agrees at
# every arm it ran at fails, with a message saying to take its line off: a fix
# cannot land without this list shrinking. A listed id that no case has fails
# `matrix::lists`. Differences that are not defects are rules in
# deliberate.toml, not lines here.
#
# A defect that shows only at some arms writes them after the number:
# `65@small-pool,sqlite-page`. The line is then stale only when the case agrees
# at one of those arms, so a cadence that runs the case only at the default arm
# does not call it fixed.

probe-temp.as.select	8	changes() after CREATE TEMP TABLE AS SELECT counts the copied rows where SQLite leaves it alone.

# Generated cases, grouped by bug. Written from the triage of an inillucent-matrix run;
# each line's case fails in the way its bug's section on task-2136 describes.
constraint-f18eefd57be9	1	COMMIT or ROLLBACK with no transaction fails with result code 21 where SQLite gives 1.
schema-013cdbdd2c4d	8	changes() or total_changes() after CREATE TABLE AS SELECT counts the copied rows where SQLite leaves them alone.
schema-4bac1079f631	21	CREATE TEMP TABLE temp.name is refused; SQLite accepts the temp qualifier.
constraint-f09d1380625f	25	changes() or total_changes() after ROLLBACK or ROLLBACK TO differs from SQLite's, which a rollback does not reset.
constraint-34e06397277a	26	With PRAGMA defer_foreign_keys set on a fresh connection, SQLite's schema load clears it and the INSERT fails before a rowid is assigned; inillucent fails at the commit and last_insert_rowid() names the row it undid.
constraint-91a394494308	26	With PRAGMA defer_foreign_keys set on a fresh connection, SQLite's schema load clears it and the INSERT fails before a rowid is assigned; inillucent fails at the commit and last_insert_rowid() names the row it undid.
constraint-ec8dae14560d	26	With PRAGMA defer_foreign_keys set on a fresh connection, SQLite's schema load clears it and the INSERT fails before a rowid is assigned; inillucent fails at the commit and last_insert_rowid() names the row it undid.
pragma-3e7b0abd2608	30	The pragma_<name> table valued function of a setting pragma is "no such table".
vtab-502dc2c0ee37	33	MATCH in this placement is refused as unsupported and no capability row says so.
vtab-6d0c72e53a98	33	MATCH in this placement is refused as unsupported and no capability row says so.
ddl_view-04962724de19	37	A STRICT table's ANY column converts text that looks like a number into a number.
ddl_view-0c7d030f2a49	37	A STRICT table's ANY column converts text that looks like a number into a number.
ddl_view-5bb6734f4135	38	Negative zero: round(-0.0) keeps the sign, a REAL column reads -0.0 back as -0.0, and an ANY or INTEGER column stores it as the integer 0; SQLite answers 0.0, 0.0 and -0.0.
ddl_view-f3ba8519d974	38	Negative zero: round(-0.0) keeps the sign, a REAL column reads -0.0 back as -0.0, and an ANY or INTEGER column stores it as the integer 0; SQLite answers 0.0, 0.0 and -0.0.

